 CODE
2.3.18.
Owned property subject to recompense 
Owned property, irrespective of the time of acquisition and subject to recompense where applicable, includes 
1¡ accessories to own property or rights; 
2¡ property transferred to one of the spouses by one of his or her ascendants either to satisfy what is owed to him or her or to pay a debt owed by the ascendant to a third party; 
3¡ the share acquired by one of the spouses in property of which he or she is already a co-owner; 
4¡ property and rights which, by the effect of real subrogation, replace own property, as well as property acquired in use or in replacement; 
5¡ the net surrender value payable, at the time of the dissolution of the plan, in respect of an individual life insurance contract entered into by one of the spouses during the plan, where the insurance benefit is not due at the time of the dissolution of the plan; 
6¡ the insurance benefit in respect of an individual life insurance contract entered into by one of the spouses during the plan, and which is due in favour of that spouse at the time of the dissolution of the plan.
